'''''Sedum oxypetalum''''', the '''dwarf tree stonecrop''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Crassulaceae]], native to Mexico.<ref name="JCRA_131813" >{{cite web |url=https://jcra.ncsu.edu/horticulture/our-plants/results-by-name-serial-number.php?serial=131813 |title=''Sedum oxypetalum'' |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2023 |website=JC Raulston Arboretum |publisher=NC State University |access-date=5 November 2023 }}</ref><ref name="POWO_275803-1" >{{cite POWO |id=275803-1 |title=''Sedum oxypetalum'' Kunth |access-date=5 November 2023 }}</ref> A semi-woody succulent shrub reaching {{cvt|0.6|m|ft|0}}, it has a tree-like growth form.<ref name="JCRA_131813" />

